  "description": "Everyday practicality with the ability to head off the beaten track. A strong Shimano drive unit with 504 Wh external battery in our low step-through frame, plus it's fully equipped with fenders, lights, lock, rack and rugged rubber.\n\nWhether your commute takes in forest trails and gravel tracks or you just want the freedom to explore at weekends, the eSPRESSO CC 400 EQ delivers all the convenience of a city e-bike with added off-road ability. That's because our low step-through frame has an easy-to-access 504 Wh battery and the latest Shimano EP6 drive unit. A suspension fork keeps you comfortable when it gets bumpy, we've fitted it with a host of kit to make city life easier and safer, with mudguards, rack, lights, lock and a kickstand as standard. A smooth-shifting Shimano 9-speed drivetrain and strong, low-maintenance hydraulic disc brakes add fuss-free control.\n\nThe eSPRESSO CC likes to show off its rugged side, with wider and grippier high-volume tyres on 650b wheels. While it's happy working hard in the urban jungle thanks to standard-fit mudguards, lights, lock, rack and kickstand, it's also capable of taking trips along forest trails and gravel tracks for fun. Featuring the super-strong low step-through frame design for rigidity, the eSPRESSO CC is equipped with an easy-to-access semi-integrated 504 Wh battery. All come with a refined but powerful Shimano EP6 STEPS pedal-assist motor, delivering 85 Nm of torque. Smooth and comfortable progress is assured with suspension forks on all models, while powerful hydraulic disc brakes allow effortless and controlled stopping. It has a high system weight of 150 kg, which means plenty of capacity for rider and luggage.",
